Subject: [PATCH] R80b, part 6, patch 8 (cld-advisor, at main's word in M16;
 main's third folder, section 6, item 4): IN A SCRIPT THAT PLANTS, A PLANT
 THAT CHANGES NOTHING STOPS THE RUN; AND A CHECK NAMES A COMMIT

Owed by main's word: in every script of main's that plants, a plant that changes nothing stops the run; and a
check names a commit, never a branch. One of main's plants at Review 80 changed nothing, and the lock's
passing was read as a finding.

WHICH SCRIPTS. A search, kept in the arc B1898 with its output, finds the tracked scripts that say they
plant, change a text and run something on it: 26, most of which only use the word. Nine plant against a lock
or a gate, and are mended:
  - B1895's runner of its eighteen plants against B1881's lock, and B1897's, which uses it: the scratch copy
    is read whole before a plant and after it, by the bytes of its files, and a plant that leaves the copy
    as it was ends the run. The control plants nothing, and must change nothing;
  - the four runners of main's unseen cases for the enforcement series (B1893's two, B1896's two): a case is
    committed in a scratch checkout, and where it had changed nothing there was nothing to commit; the
    gates were then run on the tree as it stood and the case written down as not caught. The run ends
    there now. In the two of B1896 a plant that could not be made ends the run as well;
  - main's two scripts of plants of Review 80, as mended copies in B1898 beside the files main wrote (which
    are not changed): the plants for agy-002's rows, and the five against B1881's lock.
A tenth, main's own corrected plant at the landing, stops already.

A CHECK NAMES A COMMIT: main's check of agy-002's quotations named the reader's branch, which has moved. Its
mended copy names the commit main read. The builder did not run it: it reads a file that is read through a
mask.

WHAT THE RUNS SHOWED. Every plant of B1895 (18), of B1897 (6) and of main's five changes its copy. B1895's
run: 18 of 18 caught, as its kept file. B1897's: 24 of 24, as its kept file in which plants are caught; 14
are caught by more tests than on its day, as part 2's note said. Main's five: none passes, as in part 2. No
kept case of the four runners was uncommitted (13, 3, 5 and 22).
Main's plants for agy-002's rows, each now made, in a scratch checkout: 19 of 21 answers are the ones main
kept. Two differ, and they are the two plants that had changed nothing:
  - on B1885's verdict line: main kept "passes"; made as main made it properly at the landing, the lock
    FAILS. Main knows this one;
  - "'still passes' turned into 'IS REFUSED' on the page" of B1893: main kept "PLANT NOT MADE". The page
    does not hold those words, and did not at the commit the review read. Made on the words the page has
    ("still pass"), which is the builder's reading of the plant's name, THE LOCK OF B1893 PASSES. That is a
    change the lock does not hold. It is the matter of main's row A6, which is still to build.

A test in B1895's lock holds the guard: the control, a plant whose pattern matches nothing, a file written
back as it was, a control that changes something, and each of the eighteen plants. B1898's lock holds the
mended copies and their kept runs. The four runners of the unseen cases were not run again: each case
runs every gate.

Every gate passes but the count of landings. Not checked by main.
