+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""Review 80: agy-exp's five findings on B1881's lock, made again by main's own plants.
+
+Each plant weakens B1881's script in a scratch copy of the arc so that a check can no longer fail, or its inputs are no longer
+read, while the script's output stays what it was.  The lock is then run on the copy.  A plant that passes every test is a
+weakening the lock does not hold.  The first entry plants nothing and must pass; the second is a plant B1895 already holds and
+must be caught.  Main wrote these from the reader's descriptions through the mask and ran none of its code.  Nothing in the
+repository is changed (B1895's own harness is imported for the copy and the run)."""
+# NOTE OF THE MEND, 2026-11-12 (R80b, part 6; owed by main's word in its third folder for the builder, section 6, item 4:
+# in every script of main's that plants, a plant that changes nothing stops the run; and a check names a commit, never a
+# branch).  Main's script stands as main wrote it in ../checks/, held there by its hash.  This copy differs in the marked
+# places: the lines main wrote stand after "#| ", the lines that replace them follow, to "# END OF THE MEND".  With each
+# marked block put back, and this note taken out, the file is main's, byte for byte: the arc's lock holds that.
+#   0. the repository's root was counted one folder up from the script's own, which is right where main ran it and wrong here;
+#   1. a plant is made through the guard of B1895's runner, which reads the scratch copy before and after it and stops the
